<!--
  DRR closure final-status email body per architect 2026-07-15.
  Fired twice per (customer, device, milestone): target_date-1 and target_date
  at 00:00 US/Eastern by workflow_engine.tasks.tpm_notification.

  Body composition (no "DRR closure final status for X/Y/Z" line -- subject
  already carries the routing context, per architect edit 2026-07-15):
    * Greeting to TPM by name (falls back to "TPM").
    * Aggregate summary table: Open count, Closed count, Completion Percentage.
      Closed = delivery_state in {Closed, ReadyForSubmission, SubmittedToCustomer}
      Open = all other states
      Completion% = Closed / (Open + Closed), rounded to whole percent.
    * Per-TG pending table: rows filtered to only #items_pending > 0.
      (Empty section suppressed entirely when nothing is pending.)
    * Excel attachment reference sentence.
  Signature block.
-->
<html>
<body style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">

<p>Dear {{ tpm_name or "TPM" }},</p>

<p>Please find the DRR closure final status below. Full item-level detail is
attached as an Excel report.</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0"
       style="border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0;">
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Open</td><td align="right">{{ summary.open_count }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Closed</td><td align="right">{{ summary.closed_count }}</td></tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #F4CFB1;">
      <td>Completion Percentage</td>
      <td align="right">{{ summary.completion_percent }}%</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

{% if pending_by_tg %}
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0"
       style="border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0;">
  <thead style="background-color: #F4CFB1;">
    <tr>
      <th align="left">TG Name</th>
      <th align="right">#items pending</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in pending_by_tg %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.tg_name }}</td>
      <td align="right">{{ row.pending_count }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

<p>Regards,<br/>HILDA</p>

</body>
</html>
